        <mxCell id="internalNote" value="INTERNAL TRANSITIONS&#10;The event / effect lines inside a state are UML internal transitions: the state does not exit and entry actions do not repeat.&#10;A service or save failure records the error. Only retryRequested starts another attempt. No successful hand-off is inferred from a failure.&#10;approvalStatusChecked is an explicit check event, not the passage of time. Absence of a decision is never approval. Manual takeover leaves automated release pending." style="html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=17;strokeColor=#334155;fillColor=#ffffff;spacing=10;shape=note;fillColor=#fff9e8;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1720" y="245" width="770" height="330" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vocabulary" value="ALIGNED CLASS-MODEL VOCABULARY&#10;Companion: G-04_Itinerary_Assessment_Aligned.drawio&#10;ItineraryVersion.assessmentStatus : ItineraryAssessmentStatus&#10;Draft, Validating, Infeasible, Feasible, UnderReview, RevisionRequired, AwaitingHumanReview, Reviewed, Rejected, HandedOff.&#10;The exact same ten literals are used by this state machine and the companion enumeration. TravelPlan.status : PlanStatus is independent.&#10;Alignment is implemented in the companion full class-model copy and its focused vocabulary page." style="html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=17;strokeColor=#334155;fillColor=#ffffff;spacing=10;shape=note;fillColor=#fff9e8;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1720" y="650" width="770" height="370" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="immutability" value="VERSION AND RELEASE RULES&#10;A confirmed material amendment creates a distinct successor; baseline content is not overwritten. Assessment metadata may change while confirmed itinerary content remains frozen.&#10;Invalidation marks previous review / approval as unusable for release; it preserves historical records. A later save result cannot bypass the releaseEligible guard.&#10;RevisionRequired and Infeasible conclude this candidate assessment after issue hand-off. A corrected successor starts a new assessment.&#10;Crossing connectors without a junction dot are not merged flows." style="html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=17;strokeColor=#334155;fillColor=#ffffff;spacing=10;shape=note;fillColor=#fff9e8;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1720" y="1090" width="770" height="340" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="source" value="Notation: Tutorial 7, state / internal behaviour / transition conventions.&#10;Requirements: TripMate AI.md §§3.3, 5.2, 6.2. This model covers candidate assessment and hand-off, not a booked trip lifecycle." style="html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=17;strokeColor=#334155;fillColor=#ffffff;spacing=10;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="2415" width="1550" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>